WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.280
Almost every equilibrium calculation is one of five

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:05.680
types, and what you are given, and what

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:07.840
you are asked, tells you which.

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:10.400
This video takes the three where you find

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:12.560
K, or compare with it.

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:15.040
Settled amounts, and you want K.

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:17.760
A start plus one settled value.

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:20.080
A mixture and a K, asking which way

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:21.200
it goes.

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:23.440
The other two find amounts, and they are

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:24.400
in part two.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:27.960
Type one: settled amounts.

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:32.240
A two litre vessel holds 0.300 moles of

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:36.880
sulfur dioxide, 0.150 of oxygen and

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:40.280
0.600 of sulfur trioxide.

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:44.800
K uses concentrations, so divide by two first:

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:49.440
0.150, 0.0750 and

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:52.640
0.300 moles per litre.

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:55.840
Write the expression with the coefficients as powers,

00:00:55.920 --> 00:01:00.880
not multipliers, and K is 0.300 squared,

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:06.880
over the product of 0.150 squared and 0.0750,

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:09.120
which is 53.3.

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:12.400
Use moles and you get 26.7, which is

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:12.960
wrong.

00:01:14.167 --> 00:01:17.926
Type two: a start and one settled value.

00:01:18.247 --> 00:01:23.126
Put 0.400 moles of sulfur dioxide and 0.300

00:01:23.247 --> 00:01:26.806
of oxygen in another two litre vessel, at

00:01:26.887 --> 00:01:29.286
a different temperature, and at equilibrium

00:01:29.927 --> 00:01:33.846
sulfur trioxide is 0.160 moles per litre.

00:01:34.407 --> 00:01:39.526
The start is 0.200 and 0.150 moles

00:01:39.607 --> 00:01:40.446
per litre.

00:01:40.807 --> 00:01:44.406
The measured 0.160 goes in the equilibrium row

00:01:44.567 --> 00:01:49.686
first, so sulfur trioxide's change is plus 0.160.

00:01:50.327 --> 00:01:55.366
Then the coefficients: sulfur dioxide falls 0.160 and

00:01:55.527 --> 00:01:57.126
oxygen falls half of that.

00:01:57.687 --> 00:02:04.086
The equilibrium row is 0.0400 and 0.0700,

00:02:04.167 --> 00:02:06.646
and only that row goes into K, giving

00:02:06.727 --> 00:02:08.086
229.

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:16.500
Type four: a mixture and a K, asked

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:17.380
for a direction.

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:21.140
Carbon, a solid in excess, sits with carbon

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:23.300
dioxide and carbon monoxide.

00:02:23.860 --> 00:02:29.540
K is 1.90, carbon dioxide is 0.500 moles

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:34.340
per litre and carbon monoxide is 0.800.

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:36.100
Work out Q for this mixture.

00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:37.620
Which way will it run?

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:39.460
Pause here to answer.

00:02:49.867 --> 00:02:51.226
Leave the solid out.

00:02:51.507 --> 00:02:57.306
Q is 0.800 squared over 0.500,

00:02:57.387 --> 00:03:00.306
which is 1.28, below K.

00:03:00.587 --> 00:03:03.066
That is too little product, so the forward

00:03:03.147 --> 00:03:06.506
reaction wins and carbon monoxide builds up.

00:03:06.587 --> 00:03:10.146
Q chases K: below it, Q climbs.

00:03:10.427 --> 00:03:14.186
If carbon monoxide were 1.50 moles per litre,

00:03:14.267 --> 00:03:17.506
Q would be 4.50, above K, and it

00:03:17.547 --> 00:03:18.506
would run back.

00:03:19.734 --> 00:03:20.453
Your turn.

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:23.013
A new vessel is at the same temperature

00:03:23.094 --> 00:03:25.813
as the ICE table question, where K is

00:03:25.894 --> 00:03:27.653
229.

00:03:27.734 --> 00:03:31.493
It holds 0.150 moles per litre of sulfur

00:03:31.574 --> 00:03:37.813
dioxide, 0.0750 of oxygen and 0.300

00:03:37.974 --> 00:03:41.413
of sulfur trioxide: the same concentrations as the

00:03:41.494 --> 00:03:42.693
first vessel.

00:03:42.814 --> 00:03:44.293
Which way will it run?

00:03:44.454 --> 00:03:45.733
Pause here to answer.

00:03:56.134 --> 00:03:59.093
Same concentrations as the first vessel, so the

00:03:59.214 --> 00:04:01.733
same working gives 53.3.

00:04:02.214 --> 00:04:04.933
But nothing says this mixture has settled, so

00:04:05.094 --> 00:04:07.973
53.3 is Q, not K.

00:04:08.614 --> 00:04:12.133
Q is below K, which is 229, so

00:04:12.174 --> 00:04:13.733
there is too little product.

00:04:14.214 --> 00:04:17.253
The forward reaction wins, and more sulfur trioxide

00:04:17.334 --> 00:04:17.893
forms.

00:04:18.454 --> 00:04:21.813
The slip is calling 53.3 the new K.

00:04:22.374 --> 00:04:24.853
You only calculate K from a mixture at

00:04:24.934 --> 00:04:25.973
equilibrium.

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:28.960
So read what you are given and what

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:30.320
you are asked.

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:34.800
Settled amounts: divide by the volume, find K.

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:38.280
A start and one value: ICE table, with

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:41.520
the measured value in the equilibrium row first.

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:44.320
A mixture and a K, for a direction:

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:45.360
work out Q and

00:04:45.920 --> 00:04:46.760
compare.

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:49.440
Next: K and a start, and an amount

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:50.000
added.

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:52.640
Here are the key notes.

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:54.800
Pause the video if you need more time

00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:55.680
to copy them.
